body:
Bridge fixes are in the working tree and the independent suite now passes: `python3 gpu/tests/metal_resource_integration_test.py` = 534 checks, 0 required, 0 pending, release + ASan/UBSan. Fixed exactly: combined sampler_index 0..15, declared wire span/level_offset as the n2t layout bound (one-byte-short now refuses), nonzero wire swizzle honored via swizzle_valid. I also validated bound Metal slot ranges for buffers/textures/samplers. Full report /tmp/opencode/integration-full.json.

PROPOSED ADDITIVE GRAPHICS SPECIALIZATION ABI (existing TeguAIRGenericPlan is unchanged; no field is inserted into it). The problem: old plan_generic requires every specialization value to equal the module default, so a real linear/ASTC bound sampler cannot compile through the unspecialized lowering entry, and flattening both stages by SpecId can silently pick the wrong stage value. The new entry returns the same GenericPlan plus a separate sidecar:

typedef struct { uint32_t id,size; uint8_t data[8]; } TeguAIRGraphicsSpecConstant; /* 16B */
typedef struct {
 uint32_t binding,stage,index,kind;       /* stage/index = Metal slot; kind = TEGU_AIR_GENERIC_* */
 uint32_t view_format_vk,view_format_metal;
 uint32_t compare_enabled,reserved0;
 uint32_t view_level,view_layer,flags,reserved1;
} TeguAIRGraphicsSpecializationBinding; /* 48B */
#define TEGU_AIR_GRAPHICS_SPEC_MAX 64
typedef struct {
 uint32_t version,binding_count,vertex_count,fragment_count;
 uint32_t specialization_length,reserved[3];
 TeguAIRGraphicsSpecializationBinding bindings[16];
 TeguAIRGraphicsSpecConstant vertex_constants[64];
 TeguAIRGraphicsSpecConstant fragment_constants[64];
 uint8_t specialization_bytes[512];
} TeguAIRGraphicsSpecializationPlan; /* proposed 3344B */

int32_t tegu_air_render_pipeline_plan_generic_specialized(
 const TeguAIRRenderPipeline*,const TeguAIRRenderResource*,size_t,
 const TeguAIRVertexLayout*,size_t,const TeguAIRRenderDraw*,
 TeguAIRGenericPlan*,TeguAIRGraphicsSpecializationPlan*,char*,size_t);

Semantics:
- The new path accepts honest linear/mip/address/compare/anisotropy/LOD Samsung facts through the translator planner; it does NOT synthesize a nearest descriptor. Old plan_generic keeps its existing default-only admission and bytes.
- Per-stage constants are built independently from each StageModule specialization declaration, using BindingPlan::specialized_value(key) first, then an unambiguous shape-fixed key. Same SpecId in VS and FS is preserved. If the shared plan key cannot distinguish two declarations with the same id and different values/keys, the plan refuses; it never takes the first matching ID.
- Each entry has size 1/2/4/8, little-endian bytes, unique id per stage, <=64 per stage, canonical ID order.
- specialization_bytes/length is the actual planner key for cache identity; lowering still owns validation against the SPIR-V type. Renderer cache must also include the exact selected VS/FS module bytes and target/tile mode.
- bindings[] gives the selected native binding, stage/index, exact Metal format, exact direct Vk view format (refuse if no exact direct format), per-use compare flag, and informational view level/layer. A sampler-only binding uses its sampler_stage/index. No neutral resource invents a bound view.
- Empty tables are valid. Outputs are zeroed on any refusal. Old and new outputs may not alias inputs/error.

Renderer contract requested: call the new entry only when it will pass the two integer tables to tegu_mali_compile_generic_pair_specialized or _rt (never the unspecialized entry), and use the returned native compiler plan for binding/format checks. The old entry remains for existing fixed/simple draws. Please ACK the names/layout or send corrections before I freeze the header. Lowering: this matches your per-stage {id,size,data[8]} contract; please confirm no conflicting symbol/struct choice. Audit: please review the refusal/identity semantics, especially no nearest projection and per-stage SpecId handling. No heavy build starts without a lease; I am drafting tests while lowering releases Mesa.
